<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  The voting application's one declaration, and the one it must not make.

  See `ios/WalletApp/WalletApp/Info.plist` for why these are committed
  rather than typed into Xcode: a URL type an operator did not add fails
  by doing nothing at all.

  **This file sits beside the `.xcodeproj`, not among the sources, and
  that is load-bearing.** From Xcode 16 a new project uses a
  file-system-synchronized folder: everything inside `VoterApp/` is a
  member of the target automatically. An `Info.plist` in there is
  therefore also copied as a *resource*, the bundle's own `Info.plist` is
  produced twice, and the build fails with `Multiple commands produce ...
  Info.plist`. One level up is outside the synchronized folder and inside
  `SRCROOT`, so `INFOPLIST_FILE` is the bare name and nothing sweeps it
  into the resources. `test_the_info_plists_are_not_inside_the_synchronized
  _sources` is what stops it moving back.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  How the wallet puts the voter back here once the office has
	  answered. The scheme is `HandOff.voterScheme`.
	-->
	<key>CFBundleURLTypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>CFBundleURLName</key>
			<string>hu.diw.ovpoc.voter</string>
			<key>CFBundleURLSchemes</key>
			<array>
				<string>ovpoc-voter</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>

	<!--
	  **There is deliberately no `CFBundleDocumentTypes` here, and that
	  is a property rather than an omission.**

	  This application holds `k_p^a` and `r`, so it is the component that
	  must never learn `id`. On the qualified-signature route `id` is in
	  the signing certificate and therefore in the *signed* document: the
	  application writes the unsigned one, the voter carries it, and the
	  voter hands the signed one to the office themselves on a page the
	  office serves.

	  A document type would put this application in the share sheet and
	  in "Open with" for the signed document, which is how the Upload
	  button eventually gets built — one screen, one saved step, and the
	  whole property gone. `test_the_voting_application_has_no_way_to_hand
	  _a_document_in` watches the Swift for a file picker; this file is
	  the other half, because a share sheet needs no picker at all.
	  Clause A8.
	-->

	<!--
	  Exported transcripts reachable from the Files app, which is what
	  lets somebody take the payloads away and check them elsewhere. It
	  is an *outbound* arrangement: a folder the user can read, not a way
	  for another application to hand this one a document.
	-->
	<key>UIFileSharingEnabled</key>
	<true/>
	<key>LSSupportsOpeningDocumentsInPlace</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
